      "text": [
        ": سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ اَلرَّجُلِ يَحْفِرَ اَلْبِئْرَ فِي دَارِهِ أَوْ فِي أَرْضِهِ فَقَالَ \"أَمَّا مَا حَفَرَ فِي مِلْكِهِ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْهِ ضَمَانٌ وَ أَمَّا مَا حَفَرَ فِي اَلطَّرِيقِ أَوْ فِي غَيْرِ مِلْكِهِ فَهُوَ ضَامِنٌ لِمَا يَسْقُطُ فِيهَا\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5341 - Zurah and Uthman ibn Isa narrated from Samaah, who said:\nI asked Imam (as) about a man who digs a well in his house or on his land.\nImam (as) said: \"If he digs it within his own property, there is no liability upon him. But if he digs it in a public road or in a place that does not belong to him, then he is liable for anything that falls into it.\""
        ]
      }
